Actually, it would make a lot of sense for some things to change your
charisma, too.  For example, if you get hurt so badly that your life is in
*serious* danger, you'r likely to have scars which would reduce your charisma.
Perhaps there should be a calculation based on the amount of time that you
spend below, say, half of your maximum hit points that would reduce your
charisma by one point.

It's harder to think of actions that should raise your charisma.  Since
charisma is more than good looks, however, gaining experience should have a
chance of increasing charisma.

I'd think that having an aura of blessing from your God(dess) should have a
chance of increasing your charisma.  Similiarly, being cursed should at least
sometimes be noticeable by others and hence reduce your charisma.

Maybe charisma could become a bit more dynamic.  For example, charachters with
low charisma should be more likely to offend otherwise neutral monsters into
attacking.  Charachters with high charisma should probably bump into more
'friendly', or at least neutral monsters.  

